        "description": "CC-I1 rate-list import v2: an optional per-item 'what this rate includes' text of up to 1,000 characters, stored once against one rate item of one rate-list version in a tenant table under forced RLS. The runtime may only read the table; the only write is app.import_sor_version_v2, a SECURITY DEFINER routine with v1's authority (contract.manage), practice-database refusal, MON-8 work_orders feature check, tenant lock, binding prologue and replay/conflict rules, which computes each text's hash itself. Rows are immutable and the version cannot commit without its audit event, whose payload carries only hashes. v1 (app.import_sor_version) is unchanged. A forward migration can drop the routine while keeping the rows.",
